@ \section{The image canvas}\label{sec:win-views-canvas}

The canvas has the same job as in Chapter~\ref{ch:views}: show a variant at its true scale and
let the user drag the shared line, with the same four drag modes, the same hit-test radii and the
same Shift snapping. What changes is the unit of true scale, and the gesture, which WPF doesn't
provide and which is therefore assembled from mouse events.

<<Windows/LineScope.App/Views/ImageCanvas.cs>>=
